# Project-specific additions to the generic pull/push exclude lists in
# ~/scripts (sync_common.sh, pull, push). Both pull and push honor this
# file automatically; pull_results does not, since it exists specifically
# to fetch what this file and the generic lists skip.
#
# Patterns use rsync's wildcard syntax: a bare name (no slash) matches at
# any depth, "**/" crosses directories, a single "*" does not.

# Per-run diagnostic figures generated for every experiment run (wavelet
# histograms, moment-matching plots, structure functions, etc.) — cheap
# individually but numerous, and not needed to judge run health at a
# glance the way the log/config already are. Deliberately does NOT match
# the top-level figures/ directory, which holds the actual paper figures.
#
# "**" (not a single "*") between experiments/ and figures/: since
# build_group_name() (codes/utils_experiment.py) nests seed sweeps as
# experiments/<group_name>/<config_name>/figures/, a single "*" only
# matched the old flat experiments/<config_name>/figures/ layout and
# silently stopped excluding these once the group-name folder was added
# -- "**" matches regardless of how many directory levels sit in between.
**/experiments/**/figures/
turbulence/figures/

# Heavy numeric run-output (Lagrange multiplier arrays, sampling-time
# records, entropy-bound sweeps). These are written with no file
# extension, so none of the generic extension-based excludes in `pull`
# can match them. A bare name (no slash) matches at any depth, same as
# "samples" already does in the generic list.
lagrange_multipliers
lagrange_multipliers_regularised
sampling_times
entropy_bounds
